      "<p>The <strong>Langtang Valley Trek</strong> is the closest true Himalayan valley to Kathmandu and one of the most rewarding shorter treks in Nepal. From Syabru Besi the trail follows the Langtang Khola through dense forest of oak, bamboo, and rhododendron — prime red panda habitat — before opening into a wide glacial valley of yak pastures, mani walls, and Tamang villages beneath <strong>Langtang Lirung (7,227 m)</strong>.</p><p>The valley head at <strong>Kyanjin Gompa (3,800 m)</strong> is the base for two superb day climbs: Kyanjin Ri at 4,850 m and the higher <strong>Tsergo Ri at 5,033 m</strong>, both giving panoramic views over the Langtang glaciers to the Tibetan border ranges. The valley was devastated by the 2015 earthquake and has been rebuilt by its own communities, and trekking here directly supports that recovery.</p>",
