      "<p>The <strong>Langtang Ganja La Pass Trek</strong> combines the classic Langtang valley with a genuinely demanding high crossing into Helambu. After following the Langtang Khola through forest and yak pasture to <strong>Kyanjin Gompa (3,870 m)</strong> and taking an exploration day at the valley head, the route turns south over the <strong>Ganja La Pass (5,130 m)</strong> — a steep, often snow-covered crossing that requires a rope on the descent in poor conditions.</p><p>Beyond the pass the trail drops through remote high camps at Keldang and Dhukpa, where there are no permanent lodges and the group camps, before descending into the Hyolmo Buddhist villages of Tarkeghyang and Sermathang. It is one of the few routes in Nepal that pairs a comfortable teahouse valley with a committing wilderness crossing, and it is intended for experienced trekkers rather than as a first Himalayan trip.</p>",
